     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is twice that. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Please tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, I can enter it with a note saying the dose was verified. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
